  "worked_solution": "The integral is defined over a type I region.\n\nFirst, we evaluate the inner integral by integrating with respect to $y$, treating $x$ as a constant:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{2}{\\int }_{0}^{\\sqrt{4-{x}^{2}}}y\\,dy\\,dx & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}[{\\int }_{0}^{\\sqrt{4-{x}^{2}}}y\\,dy]dx \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}{[\\frac{{y}^{2}}{2}]}_{0}^{\\sqrt{4-{x}^{2}}}\\,dx \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}(\\frac{4-{x}^{2}}{2}-0)dx \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}(2-\\frac{{x}^{2}}{2})dx\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we integrate with respect to $x:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{2}(2-\\frac{{x}^{2}}{2})dx & ={[2x-\\frac{{x}^{3}}{6}]}_{0}^{2} \\\\  & =2(2)-\\frac{{2}^{3}}{6}-0 \\\\  & =4-\\frac{4}{3} \\\\  & =\\frac{8}{3}\\end{aligned}\n$$",
  "calculator_instructions": "",
